<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 313 0 R
/E (Whenever the urban landscape alters, it continues to ascend in automobile traffic which has become an essential feature of urban life. Traditional traffic light systems that rely on fixed schedules and rudimentary timers are increasingly proving inadequate to meet the needs of modern urbanization. As cities grow, the complexity of traffic patterns also increases, lead- ing to congestion, delays and increased commuter frustration. Addressing these challenges requires a paradigm shift in traffic management systems, requiring the adoption of cutting- edge technologies to pave the way for a new era of smart solutions and adaptation.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
674 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
