/E (Convolutional Neural Networks \(CNNs\) are specialized deep learning models designed for image processing. Characterized by convolutional and pooling layers, CNNs extract hier- archical features from input images, employing non-linear activation functions for complex pattern capture. Trained through backpropagation on labeled datasets, CNNs excel in tasks like image classification and object detection. Their adaptability is showcased through trans- fer learning, enabling fine-tuning for specific tasks using pre-trained models. CNNs play a pivotal role in computer vision, driving advancements in various applications by effectively interpreting visual data.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
