/T (OpenCV \(Open Source Computer Vision Library\) is a versatile, free and open source library that focuses primarily on computer vision and image processing tasks. It provides extensive applications for image and video processing, object recognition and monitoring, machine learning, deep neural networks etc. OpenCV is written in C++ and provides interfaces to programming languages like Python, making it easier and more widely used across plat- forms and domains. It is also known for its active community support, making it a favorite of hobbyists and professionals working in realms including augmented reality, robotics and medical imaging.)
/E (OpenCV \(Open Source Computer Vision Library\) is a versatile, free and open source library that focuses primarily on computer vision and image processing tasks. It provides extensive applications for image and video processing, object recognition and monitoring, machine learning, deep neural networks etc. OpenCV is written in C++ and provides interfaces to programming languages like Python, making it easier and more widely used across plat- forms and domains. It is also known for its active community support, making it a favorite of hobbyists and professionals working in realms including augmented reality, robotics and medical imaging.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [4]
