/T (The YOLOv8 architecture consists of three key components: the backbone, neck, and head. The backbone is held responsive to extract meaningful features from the data that is feed as input, while the neck performs operations like feature fusion and contextual integration. The head is where the model produces outputs such as bounding boxes and confidence scores for object detection[12].)
/E (The YOLOv8 architecture consists of three key components: the backbone, neck, and head. The backbone is held responsive to extract meaningful features from the data that is feed as input, while the neck performs operations like feature fusion and contextual integration. The head is where the model produces outputs such as bounding boxes and confidence scores for object detection[12].)
