990 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 343 0 R
/E (In our simulation, we recreated the complexities of urban traffic using a tailored application. This virtual world featured an intersection governed by traffic signals, where vehicles of various types navigated through the junction. We meticulously adjusted parameters such as signal timings and vehicle passage durations to mirror real-world traffic scenarios accurately.)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
991 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 343 0 R
/E (Throughout the simulation, we closely observed the interaction between vehicles and traffic signals. Vehicles responded promptly to changes in signal states, adjusting their movements accordingly. Our simulation captured a range of scenarios, from vehicles queuing at red signals to smooth traffic flow during green signals and transitional periods during yellow signals. The insights gleaned from the simulation results were invaluable, providing us with a deep understanding of traffic dynamics. These findings identified areas for optimization and improvement. By refining our simulation parameters and traffic management strategies, we aim to develop more effective traffic control systems. Ultimately, our goal is to enhance road safety and alleviate congestion in urban areas.)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
992 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 343 0 R
/E (Furthermore, our simulation utilizes a dynamic vehicle counting mechanism based on vehi- cles passing through designated lines rather than tallying vehicles within predefined zones. This adaptive approach ensures that our simulation remains responsive to real-time traffic dynamics, enhancing its accuracy and utility in analyzing traffic behaviors and patterns.)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
